BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261003T170000Z
DTEND:20261003T180000Z
LOCATION:Monon South Trailhead (Salem Boxcar)\, corner of Main Street and
  W. Small Street\, Salem\, IN
SUMMARY:Reimagining Opera for Kids Presents: Ana y su sombra at the Salem
  Boxcar
DESCRIPTION:Premiered Season 2013-14​Composed by Gabriela OrtizLibretto
  by Mónica Sánchez  ​  Performed by talented musicians from Reimagini
 ng Opera for Kids (https://www.reimaginingoperaforkids.org/) in partnersh
 ip with the Indiana University Center for Rural Engagement (https://www.r
 ural.indiana.edu) and the Jacobs School of Music (https://music.indiana.e
 du/index.html)\, this engaging show features music sung in Spanish with s
 poken English narration\, making the story accessible\, interactive\, and
  fun for audiences of all ages.  ANA Y SU SOMBRA follows the story of a y
 oung girl\, Ana\, who is the daughter of diplomats to the United States. 
 Out of terrible homesickness for Mexico\, she hides herself away - howeve
 r\, her shadow wants to explore and participate in the world where they a
 re living. The two part ways over this disagreement\, and ultimately disc
 over whether they can live separately or must reconcile.Appropriate for y
 oung audiences and families | Sung in Spanish\, with English narration​
 Performance length: approx. 30 minutes
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong><em>Premiered Season 2013-14</em>
 </strong><br /><strong><em>​Composed by Gabriela Ortiz</em></strong><br
  /><strong><em>Libretto by Mónica Sánchez</em></strong><br />  ​<br /
 >  Performed by talented musicians from <a href="https://www.reimaginingo
 peraforkids.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reimagining Opera for Ki
 ds</a> in partnership with the Indiana University <a href="https://www.ru
 ral.indiana.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Center for Rural Engageme
 nt</a> and the <a href="https://music.indiana.edu/index.html" target="_bl
 ank" rel="noopener">Jacobs School of Music</a>\, this engaging show featu
 res music sung in Spanish with spoken English narration\, making the stor
 y accessible\, interactive\, and fun for audiences of all ages.</p><hr />
 <p>  ANA Y SU SOMBRA follows the story of a young girl\, Ana\, who is the
  daughter of diplomats to the United States. Out of terrible homesickness
  for Mexico\, she hides herself away - however\, her shadow wants to expl
 ore and participate in the world where they are living. The two part ways
  over this disagreement\, and ultimately discover whether they can live s
 eparately or must reconcile.</p><p><strong>Appropriate for young audience
 s and families | Sung in Spanish\, with English narration</strong><br /><
 strong>​Performance length: approx. 30 minutes</strong></p>
UID:20261003T170000Z-2418644@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260915T121807Z
