LOCATION:Auer Hall &amp\; LIVE@jacobs
SUMMARY:"Apollo e Dafne" by George Frideric Handel | Baroque Orchestra �
 � Ingrid Matthews\, director
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!About the DirectorIngrid Matthews teaches baroque violin in th
 e Historical Performance Institute at the Indiana University Jacobs Schoo
 l of Music. She served previously as music director of the Seattle Baroqu
 e Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, guest director\, and concertm
 aster for leading early music ensembles including the New York Collegium\
 , Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestr
 a\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bac
 h Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, and many others. She is als
 o a member of San Francisco-based chamber ensemble Musica Pacifica and ha
 s held teaching residencies at the University of Southern California\, Un
 iversity of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New
  England Conservatory\, and others. First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin B
 odky International Competition for Early Music\, Matthews herself has ser
 ved as a juror for competitions such as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash I
 nternational Bach Competition and the Indianapolis Early Music Competitio
 n. She has received high critical acclaim for her extensive discography\;
  her recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J.
  S. Bach was named "top recommendation for this music…on either period 
 or modern instruments" by American Record Guide\, and her recording of Bi
 agio Marini is included in the Norton Anthology of Music used by conserva
 tories and universities worldwide.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Enjoy this performance from almos
 t anywhere in the world via</strong><a href="https://liveatjacobs.music.i
 ndiana.edu/"><strong>LIVE@jacobs</strong></a><strong>!</strong><br /><br 
 /><strong>About the Director</strong><br /><br /><strong>Ingrid Matthews<
 /strong> teaches baroque violin in the Historical Performance Institute a
 t the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. She served previously as
  music director of the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as a so
 loist\, guest director\, and concertmaster for leading early music ensemb
 les including the New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\,
  Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque 
 Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Or
 chestra\, and many others. She is also a member of San Francisco-based ch
 amber ensemble Musica Pacifica and has held teaching residencies at the U
 niversity of Southern California\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin Colleg
 e\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and others. 
 First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition for E
 arly Music\, Matthews herself has served as a juror for competitions such
  as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash International Bach Competition and th
 e Indianapolis Early Music Competition. She has received high critical ac
 claim for her extensive discography\; her recording of the Sonatas and Pa
 rtitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommendati
 on for this music…on either period or modern instruments" by <em>Americ
 an Record Guide</em>\, and her recording of Biagio Marini is included in 
 the <em>Norton Anthology of Music</em> used by conservatories and univers
 ities worldwide.</p>
