SUMMARY:Careers in NYC! | A Well-Advised Lunch with Jessie Bittner and Gr
 ace Lecky
DESCRIPTION:Students\, Sign Up Here &gt\;  Jessie and Grace have forged d
 istinctive\, multifaceted careers in the performing arts and music indust
 ries. Jessie is a NYC-based singer\, actor\, multi-instrumentalist\, musi
 c director\, educator\, and songwriter. She currently serves as Assistant
  Music Director and violinist for the national tour of the Tony Award-win
 ning musical Hadestown\, while maintaining an active career as a performe
 r\, teacher\, and independent artist. After moving to New York\, Grace jo
 ined the team at the legendary Power Station at BerkleeNYC while developi
 ng her own career as a songwriter\, performer\, producer\, and audio prof
 essional. Together\, Jessie and Grace will offer valuable perspectives on
  how to build networks and creative communities\, balance multiple profes
 sional identities\, and create sustainable careers in one of the world's 
 most competitive cultural centers.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><a href="https://iubloomington.joinhandsh
 ake.com/events/2033941/share_preview"><strong>Students\, Sign Up Here &gt
 \;</strong></a></p><p>  Jessie and Grace have forged distinctive\, multif
 aceted careers in the performing arts and music industries. Jessie is a N
 YC-based singer\, actor\, multi-instrumentalist\, music director\, educat
 or\, and songwriter. She currently serves as Assistant Music Director and
  violinist for the national tour of the Tony Award-winning musical Hadest
 own\, while maintaining an active career as a performer\, teacher\, and i
 ndependent artist. After moving to New York\, Grace joined the team at th
 e legendary Power Station at BerkleeNYC while developing her own career a
 s a songwriter\, performer\, producer\, and audio professional. Together\
 , Jessie and Grace will offer valuable perspectives on how to build netwo
 rks and creative communities\, balance multiple professional identities\,
  and create sustainable careers in one of the world's most competitive cu
 ltural centers.</p>
