LOCATION:Auer Hall - IU Bloomington
GEO:39.165336;-86.517447
SUMMARY:Memory Transformed Concert: The Sway Machinery & The Immortal Kha
 zntes
DESCRIPTION:The Borns Jewish Studies Program presents the culminating con
 cert of Memory Transformed: Materials of Heritage in Jewish Eastern Europ
 ean Life\, featuring The Sway Machinery and The Immortal Khazntes.  Bring
 ing together musicians whose work engages deeply with Jewish musical trad
 itions\, the concert explores the continuing life and transformation of E
 astern European Jewish music through contemporary performance.  The conce
 rt concludes a full day of Memory Transformed programming at Indiana Univ
 ersity Bloomington\, including a symposium on Jewish cultural heritage an
 d material culture\, an afternoon reception at the Eskenazi Museum of Art
 \, and guided museum tours.Free and open to the public. Registration is e
 ncouraged but not required\; no ticket is required for entry.  Please vis
 it the Memory Transformed event webpage for the latest program and locati
 on information.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" d
 ata-start="12850" data-end="13059">  The Borns Jewish Studies Program pre
 sents the culminating concert of <em data-start="12919" data-end="12994">
 Memory Transformed: Materials of Heritage in Jewish Eastern European Life
 </em>\, featuring <strong data-start="13006" data-end="13028">The Sway Ma
 chinery</strong> and <strong data-start="13033" data-end="13058">The Immo
 rtal Khazntes</strong>.</p><p data-start="13064" data-end="13276">  Bring
 ing together musicians whose work engages deeply with Jewish musical trad
 itions\, the concert explores the continuing life and transformation of E
 astern European Jewish music through contemporary performance.</p><p data
 -start="13281" data-end="13535">  The concert concludes a full day of <em
  data-start="13317" data-end="13337">Memory Transformed</em> programming 
 at Indiana University Bloomington\, including a symposium on Jewish cultu
 ral heritage and material culture\, an afternoon reception at the Eskenaz
 i Museum of Art\, and guided museum tours.</p><p data-start="13540" data-
 end="13637"><strong>Free and open to the public. Registration is encourag
 ed but not required\; no ticket is required for entry.</strong></p><p dat
 a-start="13642" data-end="13740">  Please visit the <em>Memory Transforme
 d</em> event webpage for the latest program and location information.</p>
