 ociety of Bassists and is a D'Addario Strings artist. He plays on a doubl
 e bass once owned by the famous double bassist Domenico Dragonetti and at
 tributed to Nicolo Amati (c.1665).<br /><br /><strong>Peter Stumpf</stron
 g> is professor of music (cello) at the Indiana University Jacobs School 
 of Music. Prior to this appointment\, he was principal cellist of the Los
