LOCATION:Auer Hall
SUMMARY:Ingrid Matthews\, baroque violin
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire and additional performers to be announcedAbout the
  ArtistIngrid Matthews teaches baroque violin in the Historical Performan
 ce Institute at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. She served
  previously as music director of the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has ap
 peared as a soloist\, guest director\, and concertmaster for leading earl
 y music ensembles including the New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenbu
 rg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafel
 musik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapo
 lis Baroque Orchestra\, and many others. She is also a member of San Fran
 cisco-based chamber ensemble Musica Pacifica and has held teaching reside
 ncies at the University of Southern California\, University of Toronto\, 
 Oberlin College\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\
 , and others. First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Com
 petition for Early Music\, Matthews herself has served as a juror for com
 petitions such as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash International Bach Comp
 etition and the Indianapolis Early Music Competition. She has received hi
 gh critical acclaim for her extensive discography\; her recording of the 
 Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "to
 p recommendation for this music...on either period or modern instruments"
  by American Record Guide\, and her recording of Biagio Marini is include
 d in the Norton Anthology of Music used by conservatories and universitie
 s worldwide.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Repertoire and additional performers 
 to be announced</em><br /><br /><strong>About the Artist</strong><br /><b
 r /><strong>Ingrid Matthews</strong> teaches baroque violin in the Histor
 ical Performance Institute at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Mus
 ic. She served previously as music director of the Seattle Baroque Orches
 tra and has appeared as a soloist\, guest director\, and concertmaster fo
 r leading early music ensembles including the New York Collegium\, Austra
 lian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars 
 Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfon
 ia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, and many others. She is also a memb
 er of San Francisco-based chamber ensemble Musica Pacifica and has held t
 eaching residencies at the University of Southern California\, University
  of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New England
  Conservatory\, and others. First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky Int
 ernational Competition for Early Music\, Matthews herself has served as a
  juror for competitions such as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash Internati
 onal Bach Competition and the Indianapolis Early Music Competition. She h
 as received high critical acclaim for her extensive discography\; her rec
 ording of the Sonatas and Partitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach
  was named "top recommendation for this music...on either period or moder
 n instruments" by <em>American Record Guide</em>\, and her recording of B
 iagio Marini is included in the <em>Norton Anthology of Music</em> used b
 y conservatories and universities worldwide.</p>
