BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20261203T003000Z
DTEND:20261203T023000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall
SUMMARY:Baroque Orchestra – Ingrid Matthews\, director
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire to be announcedAbout the DirectorIngrid Matthews t
 eaches baroque violin in the Historical Performance Institute at the Indi
 ana University Jacobs School of Music. She served previously as music dir
 ector of the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as a soloist\, gu
 est director\, and concertmaster for leading early music ensembles includ
 ing the New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchestra\, Boston Ea
 rly Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra\
 , Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroque Orchestra\, 
 and many others. She is also a member of San Francisco-based chamber ense
 mble Musica Pacifica and has held teaching residencies at the University 
 of Southern California\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin College\, Cornis
 h College of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and others. First priz
 ewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition for Early Music
 \, Matthews herself has served as a juror for competitions such as the Ma
 urice and Lillian Barbash International Bach Competition and the Indianap
 olis Early Music Competition. She has received high critical acclaim for 
 her extensive discography\; her recording of the Sonatas and Partitas for
  Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommendation for thi
 s music...on either period or modern instruments" by American Record Guid
 e\, and her recording of Biagio Marini is included in the Norton Antholog
 y of Music used by conservatories and universities worldwide.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Repertoire to be announced</em><br />
 <br /><strong>About the Director</strong><br /><br /><strong>Ingrid Matth
 ews</strong> teaches baroque violin in the Historical Performance Institu
 te at the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. She served previousl
 y as music director of the Seattle Baroque Orchestra and has appeared as 
 a soloist\, guest director\, and concertmaster for leading early music en
 sembles including the New York Collegium\, Australian Brandenburg Orchest
 ra\, Boston Early Music Festival Orchestra\, Ars Lyrica\, Tafelmusik Baro
 que Orchestra\, Musica Angelica\, The Bach Sinfonia\, Indianapolis Baroqu
 e Orchestra\, and many others. She is also a member of San Francisco-base
 d chamber ensemble Musica Pacifica and has held teaching residencies at t
 he University of Southern California\, University of Toronto\, Oberlin Co
 llege\, Cornish College of the Arts\, New England Conservatory\, and othe
 rs. First prizewinner in the 1989 Erwin Bodky International Competition f
 or Early Music\, Matthews herself has served as a juror for competitions 
 such as the Maurice and Lillian Barbash International Bach Competition an
 d the Indianapolis Early Music Competition. She has received high critica
 l acclaim for her extensive discography\; her recording of the Sonatas an
 d Partitas for Unaccompanied Violin of J. S. Bach was named "top recommen
 dation for this music...on either period or modern instruments" by <em>Am
 erican Record Guide</em>\, and her recording of Biagio Marini is included
  in the <em>Norton Anthology of Music</em> used by conservatories and uni
 versities worldwide.</p>
