  47404
SUMMARY:Reimagining Opera for Kids Gala
DESCRIPTION:Premiered Season 2013-14​Composed by Gabriela OrtizLibretto
  by Mónica Sánchez  ​  Performed by talented musicians from Reimagini
 ng Opera for Kids in partnership with the Indiana University Center for R
 ural Engagement (https://www.rural.indiana.edu) and the Jacobs School of 
 Music (https://music.indiana.edu/index.html)\, this engaging show feature
 s music sung in Spanish with spoken English narration\, making the story 
 accessible\, interactive\, and fun for audiences of all ages.  ANA Y SU S
 OMBRA follows the story of a young girl\, Ana\, who is the daughter of di
 plomats to the United States. Out of terrible homesickness for Mexico\, s
 he hides herself away - however\, her shadow wants to explore and partici
 pate in the world where they are living. The two part ways over this disa
 greement\, and ultimately discover whether they can live separately or mu
 st reconcile.Appropriate for young audiences and families | Sung in Spani
 sh\, with English narration​Performance length: approx. 30 minutes
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong><em>Premiered Season 2013-14</em>
 </strong><br /><strong><em>​Composed by Gabriela Ortiz</em></strong><br
  /><strong><em>Libretto by Mónica Sánchez</em></strong><br />  ​<br /
 >  Performed by talented musicians from Reimagining Opera for Kids in par
 tnership with the Indiana University <a href="https://www.rural.indiana.e
 du" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Center for Rural Engagement</a> and th
 e <a href="https://music.indiana.edu/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noo
 pener">Jacobs School of Music</a>\, this engaging show features music sun
 g in Spanish with spoken English narration\, making the story accessible\
 , interactive\, and fun for audiences of all ages.</p><hr /><p>  ANA Y SU
  SOMBRA follows the story of a young girl\, Ana\, who is the daughter of 
 diplomats to the United States. Out of terrible homesickness for Mexico\,
  she hides herself away - however\, her shadow wants to explore and parti
 cipate in the world where they are living. The two part ways over this di
 sagreement\, and ultimately discover whether they can live separately or 
 must reconcile.</p><p><strong>Appropriate for young audiences and familie
 s | Sung in Spanish\, with English narration</strong><br /><strong>​Per
 formance length: approx. 30 minutes</strong></p>
